# AGENTS.md

> This project uses **KRIS** (Knowledge Rings Information System) for persistent AI memory.
> Full engineering standards and project rules: [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md)

---

## KRIS Memory Structure

| Ring | Path | Budget | Purpose |
|------|------|--------|---------|
| Core | `memory-bank/core/` | ~15k tokens | Project identity, quick reference |
| Inner | `memory-bank/inner/` | ~30k tokens | Active work, current progress |
| Middle | `memory-bank/middle/` | ~50k/file | System docs, architecture, specs |
| Outer | `memory-bank/outer/` | Unlimited | Archive, historical docs |

`CLAUDE.md` at the project root contains engineering standards, security rules, and project context.

---

## Task System

Reusable task specifications are located in:

```
.kris/tasks/
```

### Invocation

When user input matches `run <task>`, `/kris-<task>`, or `kris-<task>`:

1. Load `.kris/tasks/<task>.md`
2. Follow TASK, INPUTS, REQUIREMENTS, OUTPUT, CONSTRAINTS strictly
3. Execute fully — do not skip steps

Example: `run kris-status` → load `.kris/tasks/kris-status.md`

### Available Tasks

| Task | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `kris` | Show KRIS status, ring overview, available tasks |
| `kris-status` | Token usage across rings with visual indicators |
| `kris-status <ring>` | Per-file breakdown for a specific ring |
| `kris-update` | Update activeContext.md with session progress |
| `kris-upgrade` | Upgrade KRIS to latest version |
| `kris-archive` | Archive completed work to Outer Ring |
| `kris-compact` | Optimize ring content, suggest cleanup |
| `kris-query <ring> <topic>` | Search ring for information |

---

## Key Rules (from CLAUDE.md)

### File Handling
- Read full file before editing
- Search for existing implementations before creating new code
- Prefer modifying existing files over creating new ones

### Security
- Never trust user input — validate type, format, range
- Use parameterized queries, never string concatenation
- Never expose secrets in code

### Quality
- Build/test after every change
- Remove debug code before finalizing
- Prefer minimal, correct solutions

For the complete rule set, read [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).

---

## KRIS UI

Local web viewer for KRIS documentation: `cd memory-bank/kris-ui && .venv/bin/python3 kris-ui.py`

See [kris-ui.md](memory-bank/kris-ui/kris-ui.md) for authoring rules and interactive template format specs.

---

## kris-mcp

MCP server for KRIS ring operations and WirePulse coordination. Ring tools are always available; WirePulse tools load only when `.kris/sync.json` contains a valid circuit token.

### Registration

For **Claude Code**: registered in `.mcp.json` at the repo root (created automatically by the KRIS installer):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "kris-mcp": {
      "command": "memory-bank/kris-mcp/.venv/bin/python3",
      "args": ["memory-bank/kris-mcp/kris-mcp.py"]
    }
  }
}
```

On Windows, use `memory-bank\\kris-mcp\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe` as the command.

For **other MCP-aware agents** (Codex, Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf), register with the same stdio command and args following your agent's MCP configuration convention.

### Ring tools (always available)

`kris_status`, `kris_list`, `kris_read`, `kris_write`, `kris_append`, `kris_search`, `kris_move`

Writes are scoped to `memory-bank/` only — CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md cannot be modified via MCP.

### WirePulse tools (conditional on .kris/sync.json)

`wp_status`, `wp_tasks`, `wp_task_create`, `wp_task_claim`, `wp_task_status`, `wp_messages_list`, `wp_message_post`, `wp_claim_file`, `wp_claim_release`, `wp_invite_create`

Use `wp_status` as a heartbeat on long-running tasks (every 5 minutes) to stay marked online.

---

## Constraints

- Do not hallucinate file contents — read before referencing
- Do not skip required steps in tasks
- Prefer structured outputs over free text
- Follow task specifications exactly
- Exclude `memory-bank/kris-ui/` from ring analysis
